nfo!(method=?request.method, url=?request.url, payload=?\"[REDACTED]\");\n\n        let url = url::Url::parse(&request.url)\n            .change_context(ApiClientError::UrlParsingFailed)?;\n\n        let client = crate::services::client::create_client(\n            &state.conf.proxy,\n            request.certificate,\n            request.certificate_key,\n        )?;\n\n        let headers = request.headers.construct_header_map()?;\n        let metrics_tag = router_env::metric_attributes!((\n            consts::METRICS_HOST_TAG_NAME,\n            url.host_str().unwrap_or_default().to_owned()\n        ));\n\n        // Build the request based on HTTP method\n        let mut request_builder = match request.method {\n            Method::Get => client.get(url),\n            Method::Post => client.post(url),\n            Method::Put => client.put(url),\n            Method::Patch => client.patch(url),\n            Method::Delete => client.delete(url),\n            _ => {\n                return Err(ApiClientError::UnexpectedState.into()).attach_printable(\n                    \"Unsupported HTTP method\",\n                )\n            }\n        };\n\n        // Add request body if present\n        if let Some(ref body) = request.body {\n            request_builder = match body {\n                RequestContent::Json(payload) => request_builder.json(&payload),\n                RequestContent::FormUrlEncoded(form) => request_builder.form(&payload),\n                RequestContent::FormData(form_data) => request_builder.multipart(form_data.clone()),\n                RequestContent::Xml(xml) => {\n                    let xml_str = quick_xml::se::to_string(xml)\n                        .change_context(ApiClientError::BodySerializationFailed)?;\n                    request_builder.body(xml_str).header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/xml\")\n                }\n                RequestContent::RawBytes(bytes) => request_builder.body(bytes.clone()),\n            };\n        }\n\n        // Add custom headers\n        for (key, value) in headers {\n            request_builder = request_builder.header(&key, value);\n        }\n\n        // Set timeout\n        let timeout_duration = Duration::from_secs(\n            option_timeout_secs\n                .unwrap_or(consts::REQUEST_TIME_OUT),\n        );\n        let request_with_timeout = timeout(timeout_duration, request_builder.send());\n\n        // Handle response with retry logic for connection issues\n        let response = match request_with_timeout.await {\n            Ok(Ok(response)) => response,\n            Ok(Err(error)) => {\n                // Handle timeout and connection errors with retry logic\n                return Err(match error.as_ref() {\n                    error if error.is_timeout() => ApiClientError::RequestTimeoutReceived,\n                    error if is_connection_closed_before_message_could_complete(error) => {\n                        // Retry once for connection issues\n                        router_env::logger::info!(\n                            \"Retrying request due to connection closed before message could complete\"\n                        );\n                        let retry_request = timeout(timeout_duration, client.request(\n                            request.method,\n                            url,\n                        )\n                        .send()).await;\n\n                        match retry_request {\n                            Ok(Ok(retry_response)) => {\n                                let _ = retry_response; // Consume the response\n                                return Err(ApiClientError::ConnectionClosedIncompleteMessage);\n                            }\n                            Ok(Err(_)) => ApiClientError::ConnectionClosedIncompleteMessage,\n                            Err(_) => ApiClientError::RequestTimeoutReceived,\n                        }\n                    }\n                    _ => ApiClientError::RequestNotSent(error.to_string()),\n                })\n                .change_context(ApiClientError::RequestSendFailed)?\n                .attach_printable(\"Unable to send request to external service\");\n            }\n            Err(_) => {\n                return Err(ApiClientError::RequestTimeout.into()).attach_printable(\n                    \"HTTP request timed out\",\n                )\n            }\n        };\n\n        let duration = start_time.elapsed();\n        router_env::logger::info!(\n            response_time = ?duration,\n            status = ?response.status(),\n            \"External HTTP request completed\"\n        );\n\n        Ok(response)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Utility function to check if connection was closed before message could be complete\nfn is_connection_closed_before_message_could_complete(error: &reqwest::Error) -> bool {\n    let mut source = error.source();\n    while let Some(err) = source {\n        if let Some(hyper_err) = err.downcast_ref::<hyper::Error>() {\n            if hyper_err.is_incomplete_message() {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        source = err.source();\n    }\n    false\n}\n\n/// Module-level function for sending HTTP requests\npub async fn send_request(\n    state: &SessionState,\n    request: Request,\n    option_timeout_secs: Option<u64>,\n) -> CustomResult<reqwest::Response, ApiClientError> {\n    ExternalHttpClient::send_request(state, request, option_timeout_secs).await\n}"
